  "election_date": "2026-11-03",
  "description": "The 2026 election for New York's 12th Congressional District is an open-seat race following the retirement of longtime incumbent Rep. Jerrold Nadler (D), who has represented the district since 1992. The district covers Manhattan's Upper West Side, parts of Midtown East, and adjacent neighborhoods, and is one of the most reliably Democratic districts in the country, with a Cook Political Rating of Solid/Safe Democratic. A large and competitive Democratic primary field of ten candidates is vying for the nomination on June 23, 2026, with the top contenders including State Assemblymembers Alex Bores and Micah Lasher, high-profile attorney and Trump critic George Conway, and JFK's grandson Jack Schlossberg. On the Republican side, Caroline Shinkle is the presumptive nominee after running unopposed in the Republican primary.",
